+# Customer section: to confirm before Thursday
+
+- **Customer base totals by segment.** The data has new and churned counts but no total customers, so the deck gives "losses per 100 sign-ups" and no churn rate. With totals, slides 3 and 8 can show a real rate.
+- **SMB exit reasons.** Slides 4 and 7 present slower support and rising losses as a pattern, not a cause. Exit reasons, or a test on part of the SMB queue, would tell them apart.
+- **Support cost.** Call 1 asks for funding, but no cost figure is in the data, so the slide doesn't size the ask. Add one if support can provide it.
+- **Deck styling.** The slides use a neutral style. Paste them into the master QBR template if there is one.
+
+Rebuild: `python3 qbr/build_customer_section.py` · Check every figure: `python3 qbr/check_figures.py`
